<!--Workspace Documentation — TransferredSources
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.renderer.workspace.documentation.TransferredSources-->
<wsdocumentation:TransferredSources xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:render="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render"
  xmlns:wsdocumentation="com.machineblocks.bml.renderer.workspace.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Which BlockML toolchain documents were absorbed, and which were not
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Absorbed into this repository (the Markdown in blockml/docs is no longer
    the SSOT for these topics):

    - docs/05_scad_renderer.md (v2.2.0) — entire SCAD renderer spec, now
      com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.*
    - RenderEngine / MakerEngine contract and strategy text from
      docs/00_system.md (The First Engine, Engine Packages),
      docs/01_bom_core.md (Target System, RenderEngine interface, strategies,
      delegate-only targets, RenderOutput notes used by the engine),
      docs/06_compiler.md (renderer steps 9-11 as SCAD reference, Target Registry
      registration example, RenderEngine and RenderContext fields the engine
      consumes), and docs/15_dev_setup.md (engines/maker-engine layout).
      Home: org.blockml.bml.engine.blockrender.documentation.*
    - MachineBlocks host CLI notes from docs/00_system.md (Zielbild items 3-4,
      Dual CLI), docs/07_cli.md (host wiring row for MachineBlocks SCAD CLI),
      and the @blockml/cli blocks that only pointed here: DualCliModel,
      TargetBootstrap, TargetCliMatrix, Configuration fields thumbsDir /
      mbLibPath / openscadPath / activeConfig / bmlExtensions, Installation,
      PackageOwnership, LayerSeparation, ScopeExclusions item
      machineblocks-v3-scad target registration.
      Home: com.machineblocks.bml.cli.documentation.*
    - MBOM-to-SCAD serialization strategy and examples from docs/04_types.md
      section 6. Home: documentation.SerializationRules on the render target.
      Type shapes themselves stay on com.machineblocks.bml.type.*.

    Not absorbed (still owned elsewhere):

    - docs/03_mbom.md — domain object model. Narrative home is
      @machineblocks/core (com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.mbml.* and
      concept.*). This repo only restates the Set aggregations the set
      processor needs.
    - docs/04_types.md except the serialize-to-SCAD strategy above — parse
      behaviour and type inventory stay with the domain library and the
      BlockML type system.
    - Universal CLI commands, compiler facade, and toolchain targets — they
      remain org.blockml.bml.cli.* and org.blockml.bml.compiler.* in the
      blockml repository.
    - The SCAD runtime (lib/block.scad, mb_block, mb_param_*) and example
      .scad files — @machineblocks/core.

    After this transfer, blockml docs may drop the absorbed holding text.
    Universal CLI blocks may keep a one-line pointer to @machineblocks/cli;
    they should not restate the host contract.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="wsdocumentation:Introduction" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="render:README" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
</wsdocumentation:TransferredSources>
